        },
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Your stomach and intestines squeeze a lot! The squeezing moves food, air and liquid along.",
      "punch": "squeezing",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💪",
        "text": "Squeeze, squeeze!",
        "cue": "squeezing",
        "sub": "Stomach and intestines",
        "sub_cue": "stomach"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "What are intestines?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "They're long, curly tubes after your stomach. Food goes from your mouth, to your stomach, then through your intestines.",
      "board": {
        "type": "flow",
        "title": "Food trip",
        "packet": "🍎",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "👄",
            "label": "Mouth",
            "cue": "mouth"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🎒",
            "label": "Stomach",
            "cue": "stomach"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🌀",
            "label": "Intestines",
            "cue": "intestines"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So where does the rumble come from?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "When the muscles squeeze, the air and liquid inside get pushed around. Gurgle, gurgle, rumble!",
      "punch": "rumble",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🫧",
        "text": "Air + liquid = rumble",
        "cue": "air",
        "sub": "Gurgle, gurgle!",
        "sub_cue": "gurgle"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Why is it so loud when I'm hungry?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "When your stomach is empty, there's no food to muffle the sound. So the rumble sounds louder!",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Full",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🔉",
              "text": "Muffled",
              "cue": "muffle"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "Empty",
          "items": [
            {
              "icon": "🔊",
              "text": "Louder!",
              "cue": "louder"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Does my tummy talk to my brain?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Kind of! When your tummy is empty for a while, it sends signals to your brain, and you feel hungry.",
      "board": {
        "type": "transform",
        "title": "Snack time?",
        "from": {
          "icon": "🍽️",
          "label": "Empty tummy",
          "cue": "empty"
        },
        "to": {
          "icon": "🧠",
          "label": "Feel hungry",
          "cue": "hungry"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So a rumble means I need a snack?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Sometimes! But tummies can rumble after eating too, because they're always busy moving food along.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🍎",
        "text": "Rumbles anytime",
        "cue": "rumble",
        "sub": "Even after eating",
        "sub_cue": "after"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
